<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio albolineatus Schnakenberg wavelength at 37 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The steady state, Jacobian, dispersion root, critical inhibitor ratio, and equal-diffusion control are implemented and checked against the matrix eigenvalue (r = 1, RMSE ~ 1e-15). Five Lean theorems with zero sorry record the steady state, the sign of tr J and det J, the inhibitor ratio, the chronoseries order, and the k·λ product. The kinetics are generic Schnakenberg, not a transcription of Nakamasu's cell-interaction network or Volkening's three-cell iridophore model." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py L1–L16: docstring states the reduction; it is not the published cell model <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc/models/2026-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L1-L16>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio albolineatus Schnakenberg wavelength at 37 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The segmented flank has depth/length 0.221 against the FishBase landmark ratio 0.250, circularity 0.321 against 1, and structure-tensor coherency 0.360. A tighter ROI gives 0.226, so the ratio is not an artefact of one bounding box. Dispersion Pearson r = 1.000 and RMSE ~ 1e-15. The radial spectrum versus linear theory is r = 0.9799, just under 0.98, and has not yet been split into the unstable band. Kolmogorov-Smirnov distances of the final activator against a Gaussian are 0.015 (pearl danio), 0.072 (bars), 0.153 (spots). Wavelength has been measured at one noise seed." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-albolineatus-activator-ks-versus-gaussian>,
