<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio albolineatus Schnakenberg wavelength at 37 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 76/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The comparison figure places the Commons photograph beside the three simulated regimes on a shared colour scale, and the regimes are visually distinct (bars, near-blank, spots, decayed control). The growth GIF keeps the photograph and shows the cellular field in an inset because a 37 µm mode is sub-pixel on the animal. Computer-vision similarity of that GIF to the photograph is 96.0 (12 frames, 1024×680). A full-frame ablation of the cellular field alone scores 85.2. Deduction: the high GIF score is carried by the unchanged background, and the pearl-danio panel on the shared scale is almost featureless, which is the biological claim but a weak visual match to any stripe the eye expects." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py L395–L431: inset is contrast-stretched; the photograph is the canvas <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc/models/2026-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L395-L431>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Danio albolineatus Schnakenberg wavelength at 37 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Danio albolineatus)",
        "Danio albolineatus Schnakenberg wavelength at 37 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Danio albolineatus morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Danio albolineatus specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-danio-albolineatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Danio albolineatus" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Sand, plants, and the body outline are not generated by the reaction-diffusion equation.",
        "does_not_claim: The kinetics are not Patterson & Parichy's cell-by-cell model.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Identification of the assigned 3.686e-05 m scale with the pearl-danio fastest mode.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters (a, b) = (0.12, 0.88) and the diffusion ratios for the three species.",
        "reported_in_source: D. albolineatus does not build the reiterated zebrafish stripe stack (Patterson, Bain & Parichy 2014).",
        "reported_in_source: Danio patterns include vertical bars and spots, with kcnj13 implicated in D. aesculapii (Podobnik et al. 2020).",
        "reported_in_source: Short-range melanophore-xanthophore exclusion and long-range dependence (Nakamasu et al. 2009).",
        "reported_in_source: Turing dispersion relation and critical wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: Sister-species wavelengths are predictions of the diffusion change, not histological measurements at 37 µm.",
        "transfer_boundary: The aquarium photograph does not resolve 37 µm (about 150 µm per pixel along the body)." ;
